      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Mathematics and Statistics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\n\nLocation: Sioux Falls\n\nDepartment: Mathematics and Statistics  Position Type:  Adjunct Faculty/Temporary Location: Augustana University, Sioux Falls, South Dakota  Term: Spring 2027 Job Description   The Department of Mathematics and Statistics at Augustana University invites applications for adjunct faculty positions in mathematics. The department is seeking qualified instructors who can teach  Calculus I for the Spring 2027 semester . Required Qualifications A master's degree or higher in mathematics, statistics, mathematics education, data science, or a closely related field.  Demonstrated ability to teach undergraduate mathematics courses (Calculus 1) effectively.  Experience developing and assessing undergraduate student learning. Strong communication and interpersonal skills.  Responsibilities   Adjunct faculty responsibilities may include:  Teaching assigned undergraduate mathematics course.  Preparing and delivering course materials in accordance with departmental and university expectations.  Assessing student learning through assignments, examinations, projects, and other appropriate methods.  Maintaining regular office hours or availability for student consultation.   Application Materials   nterested applicants are asked to submit the application materials listed below in one document to our career center portal. If assistance is needed in the application process, please reach out to humanresources@augie.edu. Official website: augie.edu.  Applicants should also submit the materials to  mariam.khachatryan@augie.edu :  A curriculum vitae or résumé.  A cover letter describing their teaching experience and areas of expertise.  Unofficial transcripts showing relevant academic preparation.  Department Contact  Questions regarding the position may be directed to the Department of Mathematics and Statistics at  mariam.khachatryan@augie.edu .  Augustana University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Title IX Employer. Applicants must comply with the Immigration Reform and Control Act and may be required to submit official transcripts upon employment. Finalist candidates must satisfactorily complete a pre-employment background check.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=026eaaee-2102-4004-840c-8e8ad42d78b1&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201915889794_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Chapel Administrative Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\n\nLocation: Sioux Falls\n\nAugustana University (Sioux Falls, South Dakota), a university affiliated with the Evangelical Lutheran Church in America (ELCA), welcomes applications and nominations for a Chapel Administrative Specialist. This is a full-time, 10-month (August-May)  support staff position.  The Chapel Administrative Specialist is an integral part of the Faith & Spiritual Life team and works closely with the university pastors to execute programming and support the integration of faith with learning and service at Augustana. The Chapel Administrative Specialist provides comprehensive administrative and operational support for Augustana's Office of Faith & Spiritual Life. This position serves as a key point of coordination among university pastors, students, faculty and staff, alumni, congregations, ELCA partners, and campus departments. The specialist manages day-to-day office operations, scheduling and communications (including social media and web management), record keeping, financial administration, program and worship logistics, student staff support, and external church relationships while helping ensure that the Chapel remains a welcoming and well-organized center of faith and community for the university.      The Chapel Administrative Specialist interacts frequently with students, faculty and staff, guests, and community partners, serving as front-lines hospitality for the office. High emotional intelligence and leading with a spirit of service are essential. The candidate must exercise careful listening, discretion, and professionalism when triaging pastoral care needs or handling sensitive information, ensuring a welcoming and hospitable environment for people of all backgrounds and faith traditions.  The ideal candidate must be a high-capacity individual who can thrive in fast-paced settings, and a proactive professional skilled at anticipating needs and tracking complex, multi-step workflows with confidence. Key competencies include strong technical abilities (Google Workspace), proficient written and oral communication, deadline reliability, and an openness to exploring AI tools (Gemini Enterprise) to drive workflow efficiencies. Candidates must have the ability to work independently and as a part of the team, and should be open to receiving directions and feedback. Interacting with students, faculty and leadership with different backgrounds and points of view and a deep appreciation of and respect for academic values and culture must be a top value of the candidate. Application Procedure:  The position will remain open until filled. Interested applicants are asked to submit the below application materials via our Career Center Portal. If assistance is needed during the application process, please reach out to humanresources@augie.edu . Letter of interest Resume or curriculum vitae Contact information for at least three references Augustana University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Title IX Employer. Applicants must comply with the Immigration Reform and Control Act and may be required to submit official transcripts upon employment. Finalist candidates must satisfactorily complete a pre-employment background check.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=026eaaee-2102-4004-840c-8e8ad42d78b1&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201915544035_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Journalism",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\n\nLocation: Sioux Falls\n\nAugustana University invites applications for a 9-month, full-time assistant or associate journalism professor in the Department of English and Journalism beginning in August 2027.  Responsibilities: The successful applicant will demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching excellence in a liberal arts environment and will specialize in areas including basic newswriting, sports writing, public affairs reporting, media law, magazine writing and editing, and introduction to digital media. The candidate will be prepared to address the ethical uses of AI in journalism. In addition, the preferred candidate will be in charge of internships, advise publications such as the yearbook, and participate in the following initiatives as set forth by the AU 2030 Vision:  Enhance and embolden the academic enterprise through the transformational power of technology and data, and  Keep the journalism major healthy in order to sustain excellence, facilitate growth, and cultivate innovative and impactful teaching, learning, and research. The successful candidate may contribute to courses in the First-Year Seminar program, Via Viking (the core curriculum), and the Civitas Honors Program.  The typical load for members of the department is three courses per semester plus a course in two out of every three January terms.  Qualifications: Master’s with sufficient professional experience required and completed Ph.D. with professional experience preferred. Evidence of teaching excellence and scholarly productivity expected; willingness to engage in research and service; ability to work collaboratively with colleagues and a commitment to serving the campus and broader professional community. Salary: Salary and rank commensurate with qualifications and experience; excellent fringe benefits are included. Application Procedure The deadline is December 1st or until the position has been filled. Interested applicants are asked to submit the application materials listed below in one document to our career center portal. If assistance is needed in the application process, please reach out to humanresources@augie.edu. Official website: augie.edu. Questions regarding the position may be directed to Dr. Daniel Gerling, Chair of the Department of English and Journalism, daniel.gerling@augie.edu. Cover Letter Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Evidence of teaching effectiveness Research Agenda Writing sample Phone numbers and email addresses of three current professional references No more than three recommendation letters  About Augustana University Located in the growing and vibrant city of Sioux Falls, South Dakota, Augustana University has, for more than 160 years, provided a strong student-centric education based on its five core values: Christian faith, liberal arts, excellence, community, and service. The institution continues to expand its pre-professional and graduate offerings, while remaining true to its liberal arts tradition. Guided by the Viking Bold: Journey to 2030 strategic plan, Augustana seeks to grow its enrollment from just over 1,900 students to more than 3,000 undergraduate and graduate students.  Augustana offers an excellent benefit package including health insurance, dental insurance, life insurance, AD&D, short- and long-term disability, retirement plan, tuition assistance, holiday, vacation and sick pay. Augustana University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Title IX Employer. Applicants must comply with the Immigration Reform and Control Act and may be required to submit official transcripts upon employment. Finalist candidates must satisfactorily complete a pre-employment background check.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=026eaaee-2102-4004-840c-8e8ad42d78b1&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201896577033_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Recreational Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\n\nLocation: Sioux Falls\n\nAbout Augustana University: Augustana University is located in the growing and vibrant city of Sioux Falls, South Dakota, with a metro area of over 265,000 people. For more than 150 years, Augustana has provided a strong student-centric education based on its five core values: Christian faith, liberal arts, excellence, community and service. Guided by Viking Bold: The Journey to 2030 , Augustana is committed to fostering student success, leadership and meaningful community engagement. Assistant Director of Recreational Services Augustana University (SD) invites applications for the position of Assistant Director of Recreational Services. Reporting to the Director of Recreational Services, this full-time position is responsible for overseeing the university's intramural sports program, supervising and mentoring student employees, and supporting recreational programming and facility operations. The successful candidate will demonstrate strong leadership, organizational and interpersonal skills while promoting student engagement, wellness and leadership development. This position supports the department's mission of Attracting People and Building Leaders by creating inclusive recreational opportunities and meaningful experiences for the Augustana community. Duties include, but are not limited to: Direct and oversee the intramural sports program, including scheduling, staffing, officiating and special events. Recruit, train, supervise and mentor student employees, supporting the leadership development of more than 100 recreational services student staff. Coordinate marketing and promotional efforts to increase student participation through campus events, social media and other communication channels. Build relationships with students, faculty, staff and campus departments to enhance recreational programming. Assist with recreational facility operations, program planning, evaluation and departmental initiatives. Provide oversight of student office staff, projects and daily operations. Assist with staffing and coordination of the summer Kids Rec Camp. Promote a safe, welcoming and inclusive recreational environment. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree required. American Red Cross First Aid, CPR and AED certification. Strong organizational, communication and interpersonal skills. Demonstrated leadership, supervisory, coaching and mentoring abilities. Experience with computer applications, marketing, website management and social media. Understanding of student development and leadership development. Commitment to working with students within a private, church-related university environment. Ability to work a flexible schedule, including evenings and weekends. Preferred Qualifications: Degree emphasis in recreation, sport administration or a related field. Experience in intramural program management, sports officiating or scheduling. Interacting with students, faculty and leadership with different backgrounds and points of view and a deep appreciation of and respect for academic values and culture must be a top value of the candidate. Application Procedure: The position will remain open until filled. Interested applicants are asked to submit the below application materials via our Career Center Portal. If assistance is needed during the application process, please reach out to humanresources@augie.edu . Letter of interest Resume or curriculum vitae Contact information for at least three references Augustana University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Title IX Employer. Applicants must comply with the Immigration Reform and Control Act and may be required to submit official transcripts upon employment. Finalist candidates must satisfactorily complete a pre-employment background check.",
      "department": ""
