      "title": "Assistant Professor, Social Work",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-11\n\nLocation: Sioux Falls\n\nPosition Title:  MSW Program faculty, Assistant Professor of Social Work Position Type:  Full-Time Department:  Social Work  Augustana University invites applications for a MSW Program faculty at an Assistant Professor level, beginning Fall 2027 to assist in the development of our new MSW students.   Major Areas of Responsibility: The ideal candidate will demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching future social workers in the MSW program actively participating in curriculum design and development and review for the new MSW program work with the MSW Program leadership in fulfilling the program’s mission and goals enhance graduate student experience by serving as academic and career advisor during their time at Augustana University and entry into professional practice.  maintain compliance with CSWE standards for explicit/implicit curriculum, field placement, and assessment Augustana prides itself on excellent in-person classroom instruction, thus the successful applicant will demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching and mentoring students in a liberal arts environment. Required Qualifications: an MSW from a CSWE accredited school required a doctorate in social work or a closely related field required at least two years of post-MSW professional experience high degree of interest, ability and/or experience promoting cultural competency & diversity Preferred Qualifications: doctorate degree in Social Work or related discipline successful teaching experience in social work education Interacting with students, faculty, and administration with different backgrounds and points of view and a deep appreciation of and respect for academic values and shared governance must be top values of the candidate. Location:  Augustana’s location in Sioux Falls, South Dakota (www.siouxfalls.com) provides an exceptionally high quality of living in an affordable community environment. Sioux Falls has more than 70 parks, over 40 miles of greenways, a walkable downtown that features musical and cultural events, and award-winning restaurants. Our metro area (population 315,000) is one of the fastest growing regions in the country and is recognized as a major medical, retail, and financial center. If you are looking for a rewarding and dynamic career, look no further than Augustana University in Sioux Falls, SD.    Benefits:  Augustana offers an excellent benefit package including health insurance, dental insurance, life insurance, AD&D, short- and long-term disability, retirement plan, tuition assistance, holiday, vacation and sick pay. Application Procedure:  Interested applicants are asked to submit the application materials listed below in one document to our career center portal. If assistance is needed in the application process, please reach out to humanresources@augie.edu. Official website: augie.edu . a cover letter a statement of teaching philosophy copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts a curriculum vita list of 3 references Augustana University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Title IX Employer. Applicants must comply with the Immigration Reform and Control Act and may be required to submit official transcripts upon employment. Finalist candidates must satisfactorily complete a pre-employment background check.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=026eaaee-2102-4004-840c-8e8ad42d78b1&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201820178247_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Women's Club Hockey",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-10\n\nLocation: Sioux Falls\n\nAugustana University invites applications for a part-time Women’s Club Hockey Assistant Coach within Recreational Services. This position works closely with the Head Coach to support the overall operation and development of the Women’s Club Hockey program while providing a positive, competitive, and student-centered experience for club members. The Assistant Coach will assist with practices, game preparation, recruiting, player development, team supervision, and administrative functions of the program. The position will also provide on-ice instruction and player feedback, assist in evaluating opponents and developing game plans, and may serve as Head Coach when scheduling or team travel requires. Key Responsibilities: Assist the Head Coach with the day-to-day operation of the Women’s Club Hockey program. Plan and lead on-ice, position-specific sessions and assist with overall practice planning. Provide instruction, feedback, and analysis to support individual player and team development. Assist with game-day organization, preparation, assignments, and opponent evaluation. Recruit prospective student-athletes through evaluation, outreach, and relationship-building with prospective students and coaches. Supervise and provide direction to club hockey team members. Support conditioning, academic services, and other activities that contribute to the student experience and student-athlete well-being. Assist with administrative responsibilities and program operations, including appropriate fiscal management. Maintain compliance with University, Recreational Services, American Collegiate Hockey Association (ACHA), and applicable conference policies and regulations. Build collaborative relationships with students, University staff, Recreational Services staff, and other program stakeholders. Serve as Head Coach when necessary due to overlapping game or travel schedules. Perform other duties as assigned by the Head Coach. Qualifications: Required: Bachelor’s degree. Understanding of American Collegiate Hockey Association rules and regulations. Ability to work a varied schedule, including days, evenings, weekends, and holidays. Strong leadership, organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work collaboratively with students, colleagues, and other University stakeholders. Preference will be given to candidates with ice hockey coaching experience. Preferred: Previous coaching experience at the collegiate level. Experience recruiting academically qualified student-athletes. Previous experience as an ice hockey student-athlete. This is a part-time position with a schedule that varies based on the hockey season and Recreational Services programming needs. Evening and weekend availability is expected, and the position includes travel associated with competitions and recruiting.  Interacting with students, faculty and leadership with different backgrounds and points of view and a deep appreciation of and respect for academic values and culture must be a top value of the candidate. Application Procedure:  The position will remain open until filled. Interested applicants are asked to submit the below application materials via our  Career Center Portal . If assistance is needed during the application process, please reach out to  humanresources@augie.edu . Letter of interest Resume or curriculum vitae  Contact information for at least three references Augustana University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Title IX Employer. Applicants must comply with the Immigration Reform and Control Act and may be required to submit official transcripts upon employment. Finalist candidates must satisfactorily complete a pre-employment background check.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=026eaaee-2102-4004-840c-8e8ad42d78b1&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201801154652_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-01\n\nLocation: Sioux Falls\n\nAssociate Professor of Electrical Engineering (start fall 2027) Reports To:  Program Director of Engineering, Dr. Carl Olimb Position Summary The Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering is a tenure-track faculty position responsible for teaching undergraduate courses and laboratories in electrical engineering and related areas within the B.S. in Engineering program. The faculty member will contribute to curriculum development, lecture and laboratory instruction, and student design projects while supporting the growth of a new engineering program seeking ABET accreditation within a liberal arts environment. The position includes responsibilities in teaching, scholarship, and service consistent with the expectations of faculty at Augustana University. The faculty member will contribute to the development of an ABET-aligned engineering curriculum and will participate in program assessment and continuous improvement activities. Primary Responsibilities Teaching Teach and create undergraduate courses and laboratories in electrical engineering and related areas such as circuits, electronics, digital systems, or instrumentation. Contribute to introductory engineering and interdisciplinary engineering courses as needed. Develop and implement laboratory experiences that support hands-on engineering education. Mentor undergraduate students in design projects, including capstone design experiences. Advise undergraduate students in the engineering program. Program Development and Assessment Contribute to the development and implementation of the engineering curriculum. Participate in program assessment and continuous improvement activities consistent with ABET accreditation standards. Assist with development of laboratory infrastructure and instructional equipment for electrical engineering coursework with the intent of ABET accreditation. Scholarship Maintain a habit of scholarship according to Augustana’s tenure expectations. Engage undergraduate students in research, design, or applied engineering projects. Service Participate in service activities within the department, college, university, and broader professional community. Contribute to outreach and engagement with regional industry and community partners related to engineering education. Support activities that strengthen the engineering program and its connections to the liberal arts. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering or a closely related engineering discipline. Academic or industry experience aligned with appointment at the Associate level. Demonstrated ability to teach undergraduate electrical engineering courses. Ability to contribute to laboratory-based and project-based engineering instruction. Effective written and oral communication skills. Interest in interdisciplinary collaboration within a liberal arts environment. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching in an undergraduate-focused institution. Experience developing or teaching engineering laboratory courses. Experience mentoring undergraduate research or design projects. Experience in preparing for/maintaining ABET accreditation Application Procedure: Full consideration will be given to all complete applications received by 11/18/2026.  For full consideration, please submit the following materials electronically to our Career Center Portal . If assistance is needed during the application process, please reach out to humanresources@augie.edu . Application Materials: Curriculum vitae Cover letter  Statement of teaching and research interests Three letters of reference Augustana University is an Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Title IX Employer. Applicants must comply with the Immigration Reform and Control Act and may be required to submit official transcripts upon employment. Finalist candidates must satisfactorily complete a pre-employment background check.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=026eaaee-2102-4004-840c-8e8ad42d78b1&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201764583713_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Art in Digital Media",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-18\n\nLocation: Sioux Falls\n\nPosition Description The Art Department at Augustana University, a rigorous undergraduate-focused private liberal arts institution, invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty position in Digital Media beginning August 2027.  The Augustana University Art Department is a NASAD-accredited BA and BFA degree-granting program with areas including studio art, design, art education, and Pre-Architecture.  We seek a dynamic artist/designer/creative practitioner whose expertise centers on contemporary animation, motion graphics, digital compositing, rendering, immersive digital environments, and time-based media workflows. The ideal candidate will demonstrate fluency in current industry-standard software and digital production pipelines, along with strong visual storytelling, spatial thinking, and world-building sensibilities within an undergraduate liberal arts environment.  The department is particularly interested in candidates whose practice emphasizes:  Animation and motion graphics  Digital compositing and visual storytelling  Rendering and digital environment/world-building workflows  3D modeling and spatial visualization  Time-based digital media  Interactive and immersive media  Familiarity with professional workflows related to cinematic visualization, immersive environments, virtual production, game environments, digital photography, or entertainment-oriented digital pipelines is welcome.  This position is intended for candidates whose primary expertise is grounded in contemporary 3D and time-based digital media practices rather than traditional graphic design, experimental film/video, or studio photography-based practices alone.  Preferred software proficiencies may include Maya, Blender, Rhino, Cinema 4D, After Effects, Unreal Engine, Twinmotion, Houdini, Substance 3D, Adobe Creative Suite, or comparable professional tools. Experience with real-time rendering environments, immersive visualization workflows, or spatially oriented digital production pipelines is welcome.  Primary Responsibilities  Teaching digital media studio courses for B.A. and B.F.A. art majors and non-majors  Developing and expanding curriculum in digital media in collaboration with the Art Department and multimedia entrepreneurship program  Maintaining an active record of creative scholarship and/or professional practice  Advising undergraduate students  Service to the department and university community  The successful candidate will typically teach three courses per semester, including Digital Photography, Digital Media I, and Advanced Digital Media. Interim/J-term offerings may align with the candidate’s areas of expertise and specialization. The new hire will receive course-development release time during their first January term and will teach every two out of three January terms thereafter.  Qualifications MFA in Digital Media, 3D Animation, Motion Design, Multimedia, Digital Visualization, Interactive Media, or a related field required.  Professional or industry experience is strongly preferred, particularly in areas related to contemporary digital production, visualization, animation, immersive media, or professional digital content creation workflows. Previous college-level teaching experience is preferred.  The successful candidate will demonstrate:  Strong technical and conceptual fluency in contemporary digital media practices  Commitment to innovative undergraduate teaching and mentorship  Ability to teach both foundational and advanced digital workflows  Evidence of strong design sensibilities and visual communication  Interest in curriculum development and interdisciplinary collaboration  Commitment to fostering an inclusive and supportive learning environment  Appreciation for the liberal arts and student-centered education  We especially encourage applicants whose work demonstrates excellence in digital visualization, spatial/world-building practices, animation, motion design, and technologically forward studio approaches.  Salary  Salary is competitive and dependent upon qualifications; excellent benefits included.  Closing Date  Review of applications will begin September 10, 2026, and continue until the position is filled.  Application Instructions  Please submit the following materials in seperate pdfs electronically to our Career Center Portal. If assistance is needed during the application process, please reach out to  humanresources@augie.edu . Cover letter  Statement of teaching philosophy  Artist statement and description of future scholarly/research plans  Copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts  Curriculum vitae  Single PDF of 20 work samples with image list (max file size 10MB)  Single PDF of 10 student work samples with brief descriptions of assignments/projects (max file size 10MB)  Provide the names, with email and phone number, of three references Official website: www.augie.edu  Questions may be directed to:  Liz Van Westen, SHRM-CP, MSA  Sr. Employment Specialist  Human Resources | Augustana University  Office: 605-274-4107 | Fax: 605-274-5547  liz.vanwesten@augie.edu  Dr. Lindsay Twa, Art Chair twa@augie.edu | 605-274-4010  More information about the department can be found here:  https://www.augie.edu/art-department  Augustana University is an Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Title IX Employer. Applicants must comply with the Immigration Reform and Control Act and may be required to submit official transcripts upon employment. Finalist candidates must satisfactorily complete a pre-employment background check.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=026eaaee-2102-4004-840c-8e8ad42d78b1&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201747477010_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Psychology - Clinical, Counseling or Open",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-13\n\nLocation: Sioux Falls\n\nAugustana University (Sioux Falls, SD) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Psychology with expertise in Clinical or Counseling Psychology, Experimental Psychology, Health Psychology, or a different speciality that complements the department's needs (e.g., Neuroscience, Multicultural, Forensic, Environmental, or other) to begin Fall 2027. We are especially interested in candidates who are excited to teach undergraduate Research Methods. A doctoral degree in Psychology or a related area is expected by the position start date.   Teaching:  We seek candidates who are passionate about excellent undergraduate teaching. The teaching load is 3 classes in Fall, 1 class in January term, and 3 classes in Spring.  The successful candidate can expect to teach one or more courses related to their specific area(s) of expertise as well as an undergraduate course in Research Methods.    In addition, candidates applying for this position should be able to teach General Psychology and First Year Seminar or Senior Seminar.   Research: Augustana faculty have their first January, and subsequently every third January, off from teaching to use the time for professional development.  Augustana offers lab space as well as funding to support faculty research programs and travel to conferences.  AU undergraduate students who are enrolled in General Psychology courses participate in research studies conducted by faculty members. Interested students who have taken Research Methods can then also apply to help conduct research in faculty members’ labs. We work closely with our undergraduate students, serving as academic and career advisors and mentoring students in research. The ideal candidate will value serving as a mentor for undergraduate students and will have an active and productive research program that can engage students. About the Department:  The Psychology Department at Augustana University is a very collegial and supportive team of typically six full-time faculty members whose expertise spans counseling, educational, social, cognitive, and developmental psychology and neuroscience.  Psychology is popular among AU students as a major and as a minor. Students majoring in Psychology have the opportunity to graduate with an emphasis in counseling/clinical psychology, which incorporates a hands-on practicum experience at one of many locations in Sioux Falls, or with an emphasis in research, which includes a semester doing directed research in a faculty member’s lab and may include completing a culminating independent honors project. The Psychology Department faculty strongly value the liberal arts and value interdisciplinary connections in teaching and research. We contribute courses to interdisciplinary programs including the Neuroscience major/minor; as well as minors in Children & Youth; Aging Studies; Gender, Sexuality, and Women’s Studies; and Genetic Counseling.    Location:  Augustana’s location in Sioux Falls, South Dakota (check out  https://siouxfalls.com/ ) provides an exceptionally high quality of living in an affordable community environment. Sioux Falls has more than 70 parks, over 40 miles of greenways and bike paths, excellent public schools, medical/health care systems, and a walkable downtown that features musical and cultural events, a sculpture walk, and award winning restaurants. Our metro area (population about 290,000) is one of the fastest growing regions in the country.  Salary : Salary and rank commensurate with qualifications and experience; excellent fringe benefits are included. Application Procedure :  Review of applications will begin September 15, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Please submit the following materials electronically to our Career Center Portal. If assistance is needed during the application process, please reach out to  humanresources@augie.edu . Cover Letter addressing your qualifications and fit for the position as described above Curriculum Vita Teaching Philosophy Statement (sample course syllabi and evidence of teaching effectiveness are welcome if available) Research Statement that describes anticipated research activities for the next 3 years and addresses how you plan to involve undergraduate students in research Graduate school transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable) Names and contact information for at least three professional references The hiring committee will contact references of those candidates who are progressing to the next stage of consideration. At that point, reference letters will need to be sent to humanresources@augie.edu .  Contact Search Chair Ben Jeppsen (benjamin.jeppsen@augie.edu ) with questions. Augustana University is an Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Title IX Employer. Applicants must comply with the Immigration Reform and Control Act and may be required to submit official transcripts upon employment. Finalist candidates must satisfactorily complete a pre-employment background check.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=026eaaee-2102-4004-840c-8e8ad42d78b1&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201747445803_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Computer Science & Software Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-13\n\nLocation: Sioux Falls\n\nThe Augustana University Computer Science Department invites applications for tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor positions in Computer Science & Software Engineering to begin Fall 2027. We seek candidates who are passionate about undergraduate education and capable of developing and teaching a variety of core and advanced courses that support computer science and software engineering. Departmental needs include programming (various languages), algorithms and data structures, software engineering and software design, theory of computation, web application development, computer architecture, operating systems, networking, and artificial intelligence. Preference will be given to candidates with demonstrated expertise or strong interest in software engineering, algorithms, artificial intelligence, machine learning, computational theory, or emerging fields such as quantum computing. Primary duties and responsibilities include: Teaching courses in support of the University’s computer science and software engineering programs. Course assignments will depend on specialization and departmental needs. Demonstrating a record of scholarly activity and research in computer science, software engineering, or related fields. Advising and mentoring students in academic and professional development. Participating in service to the department, university, and broader community. Building partnerships with local and regional businesses and technology organizations to enhance applied learning and internship opportunities. Qualifications for this position: A PhD in computer science, software engineering, or a closely related field by the start date of the appointment is preferred. Experience teaching in computer science, software engineering, or a related area at the university level. Demonstrated teaching excellence. Evidence of scholarly achievement and a commitment to maintaining an active research agenda. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, and the ability to work collaboratively with students and colleagues. Application Procedure:  The position will remain open until filled. Interested applicants are asked to submit the below application materials via our Career Center Portal. If assistance is needed during the application process, please reach out to  humanresources@augie.edu . Letter of application statement of teaching philosophy copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts a curriculum vita  three letters of reference  Official website:  www.augie.edu Augustana University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Title IX Employer. Applicants must comply with the Immigration Reform and Control Act and may be required to submit official transcripts upon employment. Finalist candidates must satisfactorily complete a pre-employment background check.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=026eaaee-2102-4004-840c-8e8ad42d78b1&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201712573427_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, International Student Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-31\n\nLocation: Sioux Falls\n\nAugustana University invites applications for a full-time  Assistant Director for International Student Services within the De and Dave Knudson Center for Global Engagement. This position plays a vital role in supporting the success and well-being of Augustana's international student community by providing comprehensive advising, ensuring compliance with federal immigration regulations, and creating meaningful opportunities for students to engage academically, socially, and culturally. The Assistant Director also contributes to the university's broader internationalization efforts through exchange programs, custom international initiatives, and grant development. The Assistant Director serves as a Designated School Official (DSO), advising F-1 international and exchange students on immigration, cultural adjustment, and personal success while maintaining SEVIS compliance. This position develops and coordinates orientation programs, workshops, cultural programming, and student engagement initiatives, collaborates with campus partners to foster a welcoming environment for international students, and supports custom programs and international partnerships that strengthen the university's global presence. Primary responsibilities include: Serve as a Designated School Official (DSO) and maintain compliance with federal immigration regulations through accurate SEVIS record management. Advise international and exchange students regarding immigration requirements, academic success, cultural adjustment, employment regulations, and personal concerns. Coordinate international student orientation, workshops, cultural programming, field trips, and engagement activities throughout the academic year. Serve as the primary advisor for exchange student programs, including IREX and UGRAD participants. Teach or co-teach the required first-year international student success course. Coordinate and oversee custom international programs, including planning, implementation, fiscal stewardship, and assessment. Collaborate with faculty, staff, and campus partners to enhance international student support and advance the university's global engagement initiatives. Identify and pursue grant opportunities that support international education and institutional internationalization efforts. Assist with communication initiatives, including student updates and regulatory information. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications: A successful candidate will possess: U.S. citizenship or lawful permanent resident status as required by federal regulations governing Designated School Officials. Bachelor's degree and a minimum of two years of relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience advising F-1 international students, preferably within higher education. Excellent written, verbal, interpersonal, and intercultural communication skills. Strong organizational, problem-solving, and time management abilities with exceptional attention to detail. Ability to manage multiple priorities while working independently and collaboratively. Experience with Microsoft Office, Google Workspace, and student information or immigration management systems. Valid driver's license and passport. Flexibility to work evenings, weekends, and travel as needed. Preferred qualifications include: Master's degree in a related field. Three to five years of experience advising F-1 international students. Experience with SEVIS administration and immigration compliance software. Experience developing custom international programs or recruiting international students. Grant writing experience. Experience supervising student employees. Foreign language proficiency and/or experience working with multilingual populations. Experience teaching, program development, or event planning within higher education. Interacting with students, faculty, staff, and community members from a variety of cultural backgrounds while demonstrating respect for differing perspectives, academic values, and inclusive excellence must be a core value of the successful candidate. Application Procedure: The position will remain open until filled. Interested applicants are asked to submit the following application materials through Augustana University's Career Center Portal. If assistance is needed during the application process, please contact  humanresources@augie.edu . Letter of interest Resume or curriculum vitae Contact information for at least three professional references Augustana University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Title IX Employer. Applicants must comply with the Immigration Reform and Control Act and may be required to submit official transcripts upon employment. Finalist candidates must satisfactorily complete a pre-employment background check.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=026eaaee-2102-4004-840c-8e8ad42d78b1&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201711683485_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Intercultural Outreach Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-28\n\nLocation: Sioux Falls\n\nAugustana University invites applications for a full-time Intercultural Outreach Specialist within the De and Dave Knudson Center for Global Engagement. This position plays a key role in advancing the university's commitment to global learning by developing engaging educational programs, fostering intercultural understanding, and strengthening connections across campus and within the Sioux Falls community. The Intercultural Outreach Specialist leads the planning and execution of signature campus events, oversees strategic communications and marketing for the Center for Global Engagement, and collaborates with faculty, staff, students, and community partners to create meaningful intercultural experiences. This position also supports donor engagement, supervises student employees, manages communications and promotional initiatives, and contributes to the overall mission of preparing students to thrive in an increasingly interconnected world. Primary responsibilities include: Plan, coordinate, and assess educational and intercultural programming, including major campus events and community engagement initiatives. Build collaborative partnerships across campus and throughout the Sioux Falls community to support global engagement. Develop and implement communication and marketing strategies, including website content, print materials, email communications, and social media. Coordinate branding and promotional efforts for the Center for Global Engagement in partnership with University Marketing and Communications. Manage event logistics, budgets, calendars, purchasing, and administrative operations. Recruit, supervise, and mentor student employees supporting communications and outreach efforts. Support donor relations, fundraising initiatives, reporting, and special projects. Represent the Center and the university through campus committees, professional organizations, and community partnerships. Qualifications: A successful candidate will possess: Bachelor's degree in intercultural or communication studies, public relations, marketing, international education, graphic design, or a related field. Two years of experience in communications, marketing, programming, event planning, or a related field. Excellent written, verbal, and cross-cultural communication skills. Experience developing marketing campaigns and coordinating events. Proficiency with Adobe Creative Suite, Canva, web content management, and social media platforms. Strong organizational, project management, and relationship-building skills. Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with diverse stakeholders. Willingness to work evenings and weekends. Commitment to fostering intercultural learning and global engagement. Preferred qualifications include: Master's degree in a related field. Experience in higher education or international education. Experience studying, working, or living abroad. Experience supervising student employees or interns. Knowledge of a language in addition to English. Experience with fundraising, donor engagement, or university communications.  Interacting with students, faculty and leadership with different backgrounds and points of view and a deep appreciation of and respect for academic values and culture must be a top value of the candidate. Application Procedure:  The position will remain open until filled. Interested applicants are asked to submit the below application materials via our Career Center Portal. If assistance is needed during the application process, please reach out to humanresources@augie.edu . Letter of interest Resume or curriculum vitae Contact information for at least three references Augustana University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Title IX Employer. Applicants must comply with the Immigration Reform and Control Act and may be required to submit official transcripts upon employment. Finalist candidates must satisfactorily complete a pre-employment background check.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=026eaaee-2102-4004-840c-8e8ad42d78b1&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201660968458_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Cross-Country/Track & Field",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-10\n\nLocation: Sioux Falls\n\nAbout Augustana University: Augustana University is located in the growing and vibrant city of Sioux Falls, South Dakota with a metro area of over 265,000 people. Augustana University has, for more than 150 years, provided a strong student-centric education based on its five core values: Christian faith, liberal arts, excellence, community and service. Guided by Viking Bold: The Journey to 2030, the comprehensive strategic plan for Augustana University, Augustana Athletics' vision for the foreseeable future is twofold: 1. Build a nationally competitive men's hockey program that competes at the Division I level 2. Win the Division II Learfield Director's Cup celebrating broad based excellence. With the addition of the $70 million Midco Arena, Augustana Athletics launched the first collegiate hockey program in South Dakota in 2023 and is also the first athletics program to compete at Division I that calls Sioux Falls home. Currently with 21 NCAA Division II sports programs, Augustana Athletics is focused on building champions in the classroom, in competition and in the community, highlighted by three team national championships since 2016. Viking Athletics finished #7 nationally in the Division II Learfield Director’s Cup in 2021-22 and also won the Northern Sun Intercollegiate Conference (NSIC) All Sports Award.  Assistant Cross-Country/Track & Field Coach  Augustana University invites applications for the position of Assistant Coach – Cross-Country/Track & Field. This 12-month position supports all aspects of coaching the NCAA Division II Cross-Country/Track & Field program, including recruitment, game preparation, player evaluation, academic coordination, and practice/game coaching. The role involves fostering a positive training environment, promoting team building, accountability, and the well-being of student-athletes. Additional duties include assisting the head coach with day-to-day operations and managing the team, including coaching defense/offense and recruiting student-athletes. Every effort has been made to make the job description as compete as possible. However, it in no way states or implies that these are the only duties that will be required to perform. The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the position if the work is similar, related to, or is a logical assignment to the position. Duties include, but are not limited to: Support all aspects of the student-athlete development and performance of the Cross-Country/Track & Field program.  Assist in planning and implementing practice sessions and training programs for cross-country and/or track & field athletes (specific events may be assigned based on expertise: sprints, distance, jumps, throws, etc.). Assist with recruiting coordination efforts with a focus on identifying high-character, high-performance student-athletes. Assist in statistical analysis of player and team performance using film, scouting software (e.g., Hytek, MileSplit), and internal metrics. Support the development of practice plans and competition strategy.  Assist with managing team logistics, including travel planning, equipment inventory, and practice scheduling. Coordinate administrative efforts for camps/clinics.  Monitor academic progress and continuing eligibility for the Cross-Country/Track & Field program. Assist in continued development of positive public relations with alumni and the community. Abide by NCAA and NSIC rules and regulations.  Other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications:  Prior experience as a head or assistant cross-country/track & field coach is required.  A Bachelor’s Degree required.  Preferred Qualifications:  Master’s Degree preferred (Sport Administration/Management, Business Management, Coaching).  Expertise in at least multiple areas of cross-country/track& field (e.g., distance, sprinting, jumping, throwing) 1-3 years of collegiate coaching and recruiting experience preferred.  Current CPR/AED and First Aid Certification (or ability to obtain). Interacting with students, faculty and leadership with different backgrounds and points of view and a deep appreciation of and respect for academic values and culture must be a top value of the candidate. Application Procedure:  The position will remain open until filled. Interested applicants are asked to submit the below application materials via our Career Center Portal. If assistance is needed during the application process, please reach out to humanresources@augie.edu . Letter of interest Resume or curriculum vitae Contact information for at least three references Augustana University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Title IX Employer. Applicants must comply with the Immigration Reform and Control Act and may be required to submit official transcripts upon employment. Finalist candidates must satisfactorily complete a pre-employment background check.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=026eaaee-2102-4004-840c-8e8ad42d78b1&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201594396256_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Custodian, Day Shift",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-11\n\nLocation: Sioux Falls\n\nAugustana University is seeking applications for a full-time, year-round custodian position on the day shift, 7:00 a.m. to 3:30 p.m. While previous experience is beneficial, it is not a requirement for this role.   The custodian plays a vital role in maintaining the campus buildings, contributing to a learning environment that promotes health, a positive attitude, and pride among students, faculty, and staff. Major Areas of Responsibility: Maintenance and Safety: Ensure the university is in good repair, maintaining a safe, clean, and orderly environment. Keep work areas free of hazardous conditions (e.g., grease/oil spills, sawdust, excess supplies). Cleaning Schedules and Procedures: Follow daily cleaning schedules and procedures meticulously. Ensure work and assignment areas are clean and that tools, supplies, and equipment are properly stored. Supplies and Equipment: Maintain the care and use of supplies and equipment, minimizing waste and misuse. Work Area Appearance: Maintain the appearance of work areas. Chemical Handling: Use and handle chemicals, compounds, and solvents according to OSHA guidelines, adhering to all established safety procedures and precautions. Infection Control: Follow established Infection Control and Universal Precautions practices during housekeeping procedures. General Cleaning: Vacuum, dust, and clean glass surfaces. Restrooms and Laundries: Clean public restrooms, laundries, and theme houses. Supplies Management: Pick up and deliver supplies and materials as needed. Qualifications: High school diploma or GED preferred. Ability to make independent decisions, follow instructions, and accept constructive criticism. Ability to interact tactfully with personnel, students, family members, visitors, government agencies, and the general public. Interacting with students, faculty and leadership with different backgrounds and points of view and a deep appreciation of and respect for academic values and culture must be a top value of the candidate.   Benefits:  Augustana offers an excellent benefit package including health insurance, dental insurance, vision insurance, life insurance, AD&D, short- and long-term disability, a retirement plan, tuition assistance, volunteer time off, vacation, sick pay, and 14 holidays.   Application Procedure:  The position will remain open until filled. Interested applicants are asked to submit the below application materials via our Career Center Portal . If assistance is needed during the application process, please reach out to humanresources@augie.edu . Letter of interest Resume or curriculum vitae Contact information for at least three references Augustana University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Title IX Employer. Applicants must comply with the Immigration Reform and Control Act and may be required to submit official transcripts upon employment. Finalist candidates must satisfactorily complete a pre-employment background check.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=026eaaee-2102-4004-840c-8e8ad42d78b1&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200821295538_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Substitute Teacher",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-09\n\nLocation: Sioux Falls\n\nThe Augustana University Campus Learning Center invites applications for Substitute Head Teachers. The hours for this position are 7:30 am 5:30 pm Monday through Friday. This is a year-round as-needed position. These positions could occur in classrooms for children 1- to 3-year-old or in classrooms for 3- to 6-year-olds. A teaching position could be for a five-hour or eight-hour shift, and could be for one day or several days in a row. Long term summer assignments are available.  Required Qualifications: A Bachelor's Degree is preferred in Early Childhood, Elementary Education or Special Education. Interacting with students, faculty and leadership from diverse backgrounds and perspectives, along with a deep appreciation and respect for academic principles and culture, must be a top value of the candidate. Application Procedure: The position will remain open until filled. Interested applicants are asked to submit the below application materials in one document to our career center portal . If assistance is needed in the application process, please reach out to humanresources@augie.edu . Official website: augie.edu. Letter of interest Resume  Names and contact information for three professional references. Augustana University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Title IX Employer. Applicants must comply with the Immigration Reform and Control Act and may be required to submit official transcripts upon employment. Finalist candidates must satisfactorily complete a pre-employment background check.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=026eaaee-2102-4004-840c-8e8ad42d78b1&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201039623912_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Athletic Gameday Staff",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-08-01\n\nLocation: Sioux Falls\n\nPosition Title: Athletic Gameday Staff – Seasonal (Ticket Seller/Taker, Event Usher,  Event Parking Attendant, Game Day Video Production Crew, Scorer’s Table Staff) About Augustana University: Augustana University is located in the growing and vibrant city of Sioux Falls, South Dakota with a metro area of over 265,000 people. Augustana University has, for more than 150 years, provided a strong student-centric education based on its five core values: Christian faith, liberal arts, excellence, community and service. Guided by Viking Bold:  The Journey to 2030, the comprehensive strategic plan for Augustana University, Augustana Athletics' vision for the foreseeable future is twofold: 1. Build a nationally competitive men's hockey program that competes at the Division I level 2. Win the Division II Learfield Director's Cup celebrating broad based excellence. With the addition of the $70 million Midco Arena, Augustana Athletics is launched the first collegiate hockey program in South Dakota in 2023 and is also the first athletics program to compete at Division I that calls Sioux Falls home. Currently with 21 NCAA Division II sports programs, Augustana Athletics is focused on building champions in the classroom, in competition and in the community, highlighted by three team national championships since 2016.  Viking Athletics finished #7 nationally in the Division II Learfield Director’s Cup in 2021-22 and also won the Northern Sun Intercollegiate Conference (NSIC) All Sports Award.   Athletic Gameday Staff – Seasonal (Multiple Positions - Ticket Seller/Taker, Event Usher,  Event Parking Attendant, Game Day Video Production Crew, Scorer’s Table Staff )  Every effort has been made to make the job description as complete as possible. However, it in no way states or implies that these are the only duties that will be required to perform. The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the position if the work is similar, related to, or is a logical assignment to the position. Duties include, but are not limited to: Ability to work athletic seasonal competitions to include the following Augustana Athletic programs – Football Women’s Volleyball Men’s Basketball Women’s Basketball Men’s Ice Hockey Women’s Acrobatics & Tumbling Men’s Swimming & Diving Women’s Swimming & Diving Women’s Softball Baseball Ensure a safe, welcoming environment in line with facility policies. Serve in one of the following roles: Ticket Seller/Taker : Operate ticketing software to sell and scan tickets efficiently. Provide information about seating and event access, and handle guest inquiries at entry points. Event Usher : Guide guests to their correct seating, monitor assigned sections for safety and crowd control, and provide directions to amenities such as restrooms, concession stands, and merchandise areas. Serve as a primary point of contact for guest assistance within the arena. Event Parking Attendant : Oversee event parking lots, direct traffic flow, assist guests with parking instructions, and handle payment transactions as needed. Game Day Video Production Crew : Assist in live-streaming athletic events and managing game day video board content. Operate cameras, switchboards, and other production equipment under supervision. Scorer’s Table Staff : Support official game operations by managing the scoreboard, game clock, and in-game statistics. Collaborate with officials and game administration to ensure accurate and timely updates. Report attendee issues to game administration. Deliver excellent customer service to enhance guest experience. Maintain order and enforce safety rules. Required Qualifications:  No experience needed, but willing to learn. Preferred Qualifications:  Athletic Game Day Management (Ticket Seller/Taker & Ushers) : Prior experience supporting or coordinating operations during athletic events, including familiarity with venue protocols, crowd control, and customer service in a fast-paced, event-driven environment. Game Day Video Production Crew : Strongly preferred experience in video production, including live streaming, operating production cameras, and managing in-game content for video boards. Proficiency with video editing software, broadcasting equipment, and technical troubleshooting is highly valued. Scorer’s Table Staff : Experience working with in-game statistical software (e.g., NCAA Live Stats, StatCrew), radio communication systems, and scoreboard/clock operations. Attention to detail, timing accuracy, and ability to communicate effectively with officials and game administrators are essential. Interacting with students, faculty and leadership with different backgrounds and points of view and a deep appreciation of and respect for academic values and culture must be a top value of the candidate. Application Procedure:  The position will remain open until filled. Interested applicants are asked to submit the below application materials via our Career Center Portal . If assistance is needed during the application process, please reach out to humanresources@augie.edu . Letter of interest Resume or curriculum vitae Contact information for at least three references Augustana University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Title IX Employer. Applicants must comply with the Immigration Reform and Control Act and may be required to submit official transcripts upon employment. Finalist candidates must satisfactorily complete a pre-employment background check.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=026eaaee-2102-4004-840c-8e8ad42d78b1&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201934923477_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Campus Safety Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\n\nLocation: Sioux Falls\n\nAugustana University invites applications for a Campus Safety Officer, 4:00 p.m. to midnight shift.  The duties, competencies, and responsibilities of the position include but are not limited to: Patrol campus in vehicles and on foot in all weather conditions. Secure premises and personnel by patrolling property, monitoring surveillance equipment, inspecting buildings, equipment, and access points. Monitor and authorize entrance and departure of students, faculty, staff and visitors to guard against illegal or threatening activities, theft and to maintain security of premises. Observe and detect any criminal activity and/or violations of the university’s rules and regulations, as well as city, state and federal laws. Conduct investigations of incidents, including interviewing witnesses and collecting evidence. Complete detailed and accurate reports by recording observations, information, occurrences, surveillance activities, and witness interviews. Respond to unusual circumstances and secure emergency aid when needed, with moderate discretion for independent judgement. Prevents loss and damage by reporting irregularities, informing violators of policy and procedures, restraining trespassers and reporting building and facility related issues such as flooding, poor or faulty lighting, trip hazards, etc. Communicate with the Sioux Falls Police Department, Sioux Falls Fire Rescue, Patient Care Ambulance Services, Metro Communications and other Federal, State, County and local Law Enforcement agencies that provide for public safety in the immediate surrounding areas. Answer telephone calls to take messages, answer questions, and provide information to community members. Take emergency and routine calls for service, record the details of the calls, dispatch appropriate security resources (local police, fire, EMS, etc.) and provide details to those responding. Provide professional and courteous service to University visitors, callers, other agencies, and vendors. Qualifications for this position: Must possess a valid South Dakota Driver License or a valid Driver License of another state and can obtain a South Dakota Driver License. High School Diploma necessary. Prior military, law enforcement or security experience or training preferred, but not required.   Must be able to become certified in the use of an ASP baton, chemical spray, first responder emergency medical services to include the use of CPR and an AED (Automated External Defibrillator). Designated as an “essential employee”, the Officer may be required to remain on duty beyond normal shift and/or be available on a 24-hour basis to report for duty without prior notice due to emergencies or manpower shortages. What can you bring to the table? Your strong interpersonal and communication skills. Your ability to deal politely and courteously with a diverse campus population in a professional manner. Your ability to react and make appropriate/judgement calls and decisions quickly while remaining calm in dangerous, and high stress situations. Your ability to observe and recall situations and events.  Your ability to understand and carry out complex oral instructions.   Interacting with students, faculty and leadership with different backgrounds and points of view and a deep appreciation of and respect for academic values and culture must be a top value of the candidate. Interacting with students, faculty and leadership with different backgrounds and points of view and a deep appreciation of and respect for academic values and culture must be a top value of the candidate. Application Procedure:  The position will remain open until filled. Interested applicants are asked to submit the below application materials via our Career Center Portal. If assistance is needed during the application process, please reach out to humanresources@augie.edu . Letter of interest Resume or curriculum vitae Contact information for at least three references Augustana University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Title IX Employer. Applicants must comply with the Immigration Reform and Control Act and may be required to submit official transcripts upon employment. Finalist candidates must satisfactorily complete a pre-employment background check.",
      "department": ""
    }
  },
